/-!
# Full faithfulness of `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a` on the small étale site

Stacks 0GN7 and clause (1) of Stacks 06VE assert that `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a` is fully faithful as a functor
out of `QCoh(𝒪_S)`, and each of them asserts it of **two** functors: one into the modules on a
big site `(Sch/S)_τ`, one into the modules on a small site `S_τ`.  The big-site half, at all five
`τ` and with no hypothesis, is
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.AssociatedModule.BaseFullyFaithful`.  This file is about
the small-site half at `τ = étale`, whose functor is Definition 03DU (4),
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.associatedModule`.

Full faithfulness of a left adjoint composed with the inclusion of a full subcategory *is* the
unit of the adjunction being an isomorphism at the objects of that subcategory, and the
categorical half of that is topology-free and already isolated:
`CategoryTheory.Adjunction.full_comp_L_of_isIso_unit_app` and
`CategoryTheory.Adjunction.faithful_comp_L_of_mono_unit_app`.  So the whole of the small-site
half of the two tags is the one statement `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.UnitIsoOnQuasicoherent`:
the unit `𝓕 ⟶ (𝓕^a)|_{S_Zar}` of `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.associatedModuleAdjunction` is an
isomorphism at every quasi-coherent `𝒪_S`-module.

**This file proves that statement at every *free* `𝒪_S`-module, with no hypothesis on `S`**, and
records what remains.  The argument is the one the big fppf site uses
(`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isIso_unit_app_free`): the generic
`SheafOfModules.isIso_toSheaf_map_unit_app_free_app` makes the unit at `free I` an isomorphism on
sections at any object `T` of the source site which is a quasi-compact object there, whose image
downstairs is a quasi-compact object, and at which the comparison of structure sheaves is an
isomorphism; the affine opens of `S` are such objects and they form a basis of the Zariski
topology, so the unit is an isomorphism of Zariski sheaves.

The one input that the small étale site did not have is **quasi-compactness of its objects**,
Stacks 090H, and supplying it is most of this file.  The big-site route is unavailable: the big
fppf site of `S` is a *localization*, so
`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.isQuasiCompactObject_over` carries the statement down from
the ambient category of schemes, whereas the small étale site is
a full subcategory cut out by an object property and its topology is generated by its own
covering families, which carry a cardinality bound.  The argument is therefore run on the small
étale site directly, and it is the one the source gives: a covering sieve contains a chosen
covering family, whose members are étale hence open and jointly surjective, so finitely many of
their images already cover a quasi-compact object, and the finite subfamily is again a covering
family — the cardinality bound being settled by
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.presieve₀_mem_precoverage_of_jointlySurjective`, which absorbs
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigEtaleSite.exists_covering_rep`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.UnitIsoOnQuasicoherent`: the single statement the small-site half
  of Stacks 0GN7 and of Stacks 06VE (1) reduces to.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.SectionsComparisonSheafifiesToIso`: **Stacks 070S part (2) for
  `S_étale`**, which is the single thing that statement needs beyond this file.  It is proved,
  downstream, in
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.AssociatedModule.SmallEtaleLocalBijectivity`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.presieve₀_mem_precoverage_of_jointlySurjective`: a jointly
  surjective family of the small étale site of `S` is a covering family.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.exists_isCovering_sieve₀_le` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.jointlySurjective_of_isCovering`: a covering sieve of the small
  étale site contains a covering family, and a covering family is jointly surjective.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isQuasiCompactObject_of_compactSpace`: **Stacks 090H for the
  small étale site** — an object whose underlying scheme is quasi-compact is a quasi-compact
  object of the site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isIso_unit_app_free`: **the unit of the associated-module
  adjunction of `S_étale` is an isomorphism at every free `𝒪_S`-module**, for every `S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.bijective_associatedModule_map_free`: **Stacks 06VE (1) on the
  small étale site with free target** — `Hom(𝓕, ⊕_I 𝒪_S) ⟶ Hom(𝓕^a, ⊕_I 𝒪)` is bijective for
  every `𝒪_S`-module `𝓕`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.full_associatedModuleQcoh`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.faithful_associatedModuleQcoh` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.fullyFaithfulAssociatedModuleQcoh`: the small-site half of
  Stacks 0GN7 and of Stacks 06VE (1) at `τ = étale`, over
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.UnitIsoOnQuasicoherent`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.unitIsoOnQuasicoherent_of_sectionsComparison` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.fullyFaithfulAssociatedModuleQcoh_of_sectionsComparison`: the
  same, over **Stacks 070S part (2) alone** — the sharpest hypothesis-carrying form.  The
  hypothesis-free forms, obtained by feeding
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.sectionsComparisonSheafifiesToIso` to these, are in
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.AssociatedModule.SmallEtaleLocalBijectivity`.

## Implementation notes

**Nothing here is tagged**, and the reason is R56: every statement of the last group carries the
hypothesis `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.UnitIsoOnQuasicoherent`, and a hypothesis is part of a
citation.  The free case is not a clause of either tag, so it is not taggable either: 06VE (1)
and 0GN7 quantify over all quasi-coherent `𝓕`, and a free module is one of those.

**What is missing, as one declaration.**  `UnitIsoOnQuasicoherent` does *not* follow from the
free case, and the obstruction is the same structural one recorded on
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.UnitIsoOnQuasicoherent`: presenting a quasi-coherent `𝓕` as a
cokernel of free modules carries over to `𝓕^a` because `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a` is a left adjoint, but
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.restrictModule` is a *right* adjoint, so the unit at `𝓕` is not
determined by the unit at the free modules.  The route the source takes instead is through the
*sections* description of `𝓕^a` — Definition 03DU (4) together with Stacks 070S — and at the big
site that route is `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.AssociatedModule.UnitQuasicoherent`,
which proves the unit is an isomorphism out of exactly three inputs: that pulling sections back
is an isomorphism, that the pullback-sections presheaf is a sheaf (Stacks 03DT), and that the
sheafification of the comparison between the presheaf-level pullback and the pullback-sections
presheaf is an isomorphism (Stacks 070S).

**Two of those three now hold on the small étale site**, in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.AssociatedModule.SmallEtaleSectionsComparison`:
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isIso_sectionsUnit` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isSheaf_sectionsPresheafOfModules`, the latter being **Stacks 03DT
on the small étale site with no hypothesis**.  So
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isIso_unit_app_of_isIso_sheafification_sectionsComparison` carries
the third as its only hypothesis, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.unitIsoOnQuasicoherent_of_sectionsComparison` below turns it into
`UnitIsoOnQuasicoherent`.

**The third input is Stacks 070S part (2) for `S_étale`**, named here as
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.SectionsComparisonSheafifiesToIso`: local bijectivity, for
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.topology`, of `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.sectionsComparison` —
the small étale analogue of the pair
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isLocallySurjective_sectionsComparison_baseOverTopology` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isLocallyInjective_sectionsComparison_baseOverTopology`, from
which `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.baseAssociatedModuleIsoSections` is assembled.  It is
proved in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Descent/AssociatedModule/SmallEtaleLocalBijectivity.lean`:
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.sectionsComparisonSheafifiesToIso` is a theorem with no
hypothesis.  The small étale `070S` attribute sits on the form of it with no hypothesis on `𝓕`
either, `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isIso_sheafification_map_sectionsComparison`, the source
stating part (2) for an arbitrary sheaf of `𝒪_S`-modules.  The statements here that take the
predicate as a hypothesis therefore have unconditional forms beside them in that file —
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.unitIsoOnQuasicoherent`, `full_associatedModuleQcoh'` and
`faithful_associatedModuleQcoh'` — and a reader should use those.  It is stated as a named
proposition here all the same, because this file is upstream of its proof and the statements
above are the ones it feeds.

**A generalization, not a second copy.**  `presieve₀_mem_precoverage_of_jointlySurjective` below
generalizes `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.presieve₀_mem_precoverage_of_isOpenImmersion`
(`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Descent/AssociatedModule/SmallEtaleRingedSite.lean:246`), whose
open-immersion hypothesis is used for nothing but deriving `AlgebraicGeometry.Etale` of each
member — and every morphism of the small étale site is étale anyway, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.etale_toScheme_map` of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.SupportSections`.
The general form is written here rather than in the pre-existing file, and the older
statement is left untouched, to be re-expressed as its instance; the two are not unrelated
copies.

**A restatement at a variable morphism, not a raised elaboration budget.**  In
`isQuasiCompactObject_of_compactSpace` the open cover is indexed by
`fun i => Set.range ⇑((toScheme B S hS).map (E.f i))` rather than by
`fun i => Set.range ⇑((PreZeroHypercover.map (toScheme B S hS) E).f i)`.  The two are
definitionally equal, but the second is a projection out of a structure literal and instance
search does not reduce it, so `AlgebraicGeometry.UniversallyOpen` is not found at that spelling
even though `etale_toScheme_map` supplies it at the first.  Stating the cover at the variable
morphism costs nothing.

